<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomPermission xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, DELIBERATELY. CustomPermission's
        <description> is capped at 255 characters (measured on this project 2026-08-12 via
        Disposition_Deal_Actions.customPermission-meta.xml's own first-draft dry-run failure). A
        comment is repo-only and never sent to the Metadata API, so it can be as long as it needs.

        DISPOSITION GAP CLOSURE TRANCHE 2, ITEM 5a (agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t2-design.md
        §3 item 5a; Gate 1 decisions D-9 and D-10, 2026-08-31). NEW custom permission gating
        visibility of, and server-side access to, the Sell Meter "Override" action on a YELLOW-band
        Property_Asset__c (stories 12/14). Granted by DPEG_Disposition_View ONLY — the Principal
        persona, reaching every holder of DPEG_Principal_PSG.

        🔴 THIS TOKEN IS THE MIRROR IMAGE OF Disposition_Deal_Actions AND THE TWO MUST NEVER BE
        MERGED. Quoting Disposition_Deal_Actions.customPermission-meta.xml's own banner verbatim,
        because the request that produced this file originally cited Disposition_Deal_Actions as
        its precedent and that token is PRECISELY THE WRONG ONE to reuse or to mirror onto the same
        set (design finding P-5, "the single most consequential correction in this document"):

            "🔴 DPEG_Disposition_View DOES NOT AND MUST NOT CARRY THIS PERMISSION. Principals hold
            the View set and APPROVE dispositions; granting it there would put the submit and
            advance buttons in front of the approvers of those submissions. The two disposition
            sets are deliberately asymmetric on this grant."

        That banner is about Disposition_Deal_Actions, which lives on DPEG_Disposition_Edit (the
        ANALYST set) and is FORBIDDEN on DPEG_Disposition_View (the PRINCIPAL set). THIS token,
        Disposition_Sell_Meter_Override, is the exact inverse: it lives on DPEG_Disposition_View
        (Principal) and must NOT be added to DPEG_Disposition_Edit. Reusing Disposition_Deal_Actions
        for this gate, or granting THIS token symmetrically onto DPEG_Disposition_Edit "to match",
        would show the Override action to analysts and hide it from principals — the acceptance
        criteria for stories 12/14, exactly inverted. The two tokens are deliberate mirror images;
        merging or symmetrising them collapses whichever gate is touched.

        SCOPE: fires only on the YELLOW band (days-until-peak 31-90 via SellMeterService.
        bandForPeak). GREEN Initiate stays open to every junior analyst — no story asks to close it
        — and RED stays refused to everyone via the existing SellMeterGateException path. The
        server-side assert lives on BOTH DispositionService create paths (findOrCreate AND
        initiateAndSubmit), per DispositionService.cls's own pre-written condition for flipping its
        recorded refusal to assert here at all. That Apex change is OWNED BY salesforce-developer,
        not this file — this file only defines the token.

        FLS / assignment: DPEG_Disposition_View's <customPermissions> entry naming this token, and
        the fieldPermissions grant on the new Disposition__c.Sell_Meter_Override_Reason__c field,
        are a SEPARATE, consolidated pass owned by salesforce-solution-architect (design §4) — NOT
        this file, and NOT DPEG_Disposition_Edit. "The four principals" who end up holding this
        token is a PermissionSetAssignment question and assignments are not deployable metadata;
        the deliverable here is "whoever holds DPEG_Principal_PSG", verified in the org, not in
        this repo.

        🔴 DEPLOY ORDER: this file must land in the SAME deploy as, or an EARLIER deploy than,
        DPEG_Disposition_View.permissionset-meta.xml. A customPermissions entry naming a permission
        the target org does not yet hold fails the deploy of the entire permission set (precedent:
        DPEG_Admin_Access's Tranche 1 header).

        isLicensed=false — no managed-package license gating; this is an in-org, purely
        criteria-based (does the running user hold this token?) authorization gate, not a
        record-based one. FeatureManagement.checkPermission is the intended server-side check.
    -->
    <label>Disposition Sell Meter Override</label>
    <description>Layer-5 authorization token gating the Sell Meter Override action on a YELLOW-band Disposition asset. Granted by DPEG_Disposition_View (Principal) ONLY - never DPEG_Disposition_Edit. See this file's XML comment.</description>
    <isLicensed>false</isLicensed>
</CustomPermission>
